# Do tanglefoot strands catch the MOUNT and leave the rider free? (bd inc-lxvv)
#
# THE DEFECT. The terrain's EV_MOVE handler (lib/alchemy.irh) makes the MOUNT
# roll the reflex save when a mounted creature moves in the strands, which is
# right -- it is the mount's legs in the strands. The consequence went to the
# wrong creature: the original tail ran ThrowDmg(...,EActor,EActor), so the
# RIDER took AD_STUK for a save the MOUNT had failed. A level-1 paladin on his
# sacred mount stood on the strands with "Stuck" on his own status line while
# the horse under him was free to walk.
#
# WHERE THE ROLL HAPPENS, because it is not where a reader expects. The
# terrain sees EV_MOVE at the square the creature is STANDING ON, not the one
# it is entering (src/Event.cpp:184-198 takes tx,ty from the actor, and the
# move event is thrown before the actor is relocated). So the strands catch a
# creature that tries to LEAVE them, which is what the terrain's own Desc says:
# "A creature attempting to move or attack in the strands must make a reflex
# saving throw (DC 15) to avoid becoming stuck instead." That is why this
# script lays a STRIP of strands and rides along it: stepping onto the first
# square rolls nothing, and each step after that rolls once.
#
# THE RIDE, on seed 4 under tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat:
#
#   step 1  cave entrance -> strands 1   no roll (he was not in the strands)
#   step 2  strands 1 -> strands 2       Keeper's Reflex Save 20+1 = 21, success
#                                        -> "Keeper seems to be entangled."
#   step 3  strands 2 -> strands 3       Keeper's Reflex Save 14 vs DC 15,
#                                        FAILURE -> the mount is stuck, the
#                                        move is refused, and the pair stay on
#                                        strands 2
#
# Five strands squares are laid rather than three so that step 3 is a move
# from strands INTO strands. A step off the end of the strip would roll too,
# but it would also put the pair on clear ground, and the interesting state is
# a stuck mount standing in the hazard.
#
# THE ORACLE is wizard mode's "Examine Player Data", which prints the rider's
# whole stati list and then, under a "----MOUNT----" banner, the mount's
# (src/Debug.cpp:1713-1718). Two screens are dumped out of that one scrolling
# window, because the two stati lists are 120 lines apart:
#
#   rider-stati   20 lines down: the rider's "Stati (7):" list entire, from
#                 EXTRA SKILL to ALIGNMENT, ending at "Inventory:". The
#                 MOUNTED entry naming Keeper is what says whose list it is.
#   mount-stati   140 lines down: "----MOUNT----", "horse named Keeper", and
#                 the mount's own "Stati (6):" list with STUCK in it, all on
#                 one screen. 150 is too far -- the banner has scrolled off by
#                 then -- so this depth is pinned, not approximate.
#
# The map screen dumped as "crossed" carries the same finding in the player's
# own words: his status line must not say Stuck while "Keeper seems to be
# stuck." stands on the message line.
#
# Freeze Monsters is on so that nothing walks into the strip or onto the
# message line while the pair are riding.
#
# Read by tools/check_tanglefoot_mount.sh.

@include chargen-paladin.keys
@until "Afoot" ESC

w       # wizard mode
y       # "Enter wizard mode?" -- yes
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN*10 # Freeze Monsters is the eleventh row; the cursor opens on the first
SPACE   # Freeze Monsters: NO -> YES
ESC

# Climb on. chargen-paladin.keys' header records that the sacred mount is the
# 'q' immediately WEST of the '@' on this seed.
y
@choose "Mount"
LEFT ENTER
@dump:mounted
SPACE SPACE

# Lay five squares of tanglefoot strands east of the entrance. The wizard
# location prompt opens on the player, so N presses of RIGHT name the square
# N east of him. TAB pages the terrain menu; "tanglefoot strands" is on the
# second page.
w
@choose "Change terrain type"
RIGHT
ENTER
TAB
@choose "tanglefoot strands"
w
@choose "Change terrain type"
RIGHT RIGHT
ENTER
TAB
@choose "tanglefoot strands"
w
@choose "Change terrain type"
RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT
ENTER
TAB
@choose "tanglefoot strands"
w
@choose "Change terrain type"
RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT
ENTER
TAB
@choose "tanglefoot strands"
w
@choose "Change terrain type"
RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT
ENTER
TAB
@choose "tanglefoot strands"
@dump:terrain-made

# Ride east. The first step asks for confirmation, because the terrain under
# the destination differs from the terrain under the pair and the strands
# carry TF_WARN (src/Move.cpp:576-581). The two steps after it do not: strands
# to strands is no change of terrain.
RIGHT
@while "Confirm" y
RIGHT
@while "Confirm" y
RIGHT
@while "Confirm" y
@dump:crossed

SPACE SPACE
w
@choose "Examine Player Data"
DOWN*20
@dump:rider-stati
DOWN*120
@dump:mount-stati
ESC
@quit
